1
00:01:47,973 --> 00:01:49,500
You're special.

2
00:01:50,724 --> 00:01:54,204
You have a very special
purpose in life.

3
00:01:56,420 --> 00:01:57,827
You've been chosen.

4
00:02:08,803 --> 00:02:11,170
The Island awaits you.

5
00:02:59,200 --> 00:03:01,982
I'm fine, I'm fine, I'm fine.

6
00:03:28,894 --> 00:03:30,781
Good morning, Tower One.

7
00:03:30,846 --> 00:03:34,293
Exterior contamination index
is 85 percent.

8
00:03:34,366 --> 00:03:35,795
Sunny and mild.

9
00:03:46,461 --> 00:03:48,370
Hey, I'm missing a left shoe.

10
00:03:51,772 --> 00:03:54,554
And when you get a chance,
I'd like another color.

11
00:04:04,988 --> 00:04:07,355
- Morning.
- Good morning.

12
00:04:15,003 --> 00:04:18,100
- Hey, Lincoln. How you doing?
- I'm missing a shoe.

13
00:04:28,090 --> 00:04:30,773
- Hey, you're cutting.
- Yeah.

14
00:04:31,962 --> 00:04:33,489
Thank you.

15
00:04:34,586 --> 00:04:36,342
We're full.

16
00:04:39,386 --> 00:04:42,899
Good morning.
July 19th, 2019.

17
00:04:42,970 --> 00:04:45,141
Another day in paradise.

18
00:04:58,456 --> 00:05:00,595
Starkweather Two Delta,

19
00:05:00,665 --> 00:05:01,974
your time has come.

20
00:05:02,040 --> 00:05:04,887
You're moving out to the Island.

21
00:05:04,952 --> 00:05:06,839
Starkweather Two Delta here.

22
00:05:06,904 --> 00:05:10,165
And, as you know, the biggest dream
of my life just came true.

23
00:05:10,231 --> 00:05:12,849
I've only been with you guys
for, like, six months,

24
00:05:12,919 --> 00:05:14,610
but I won the lottery.

25
00:05:14,679 --> 00:05:17,199
- That's right, me, Starkweather, OK?
- Six months.

26
00:05:17,271 --> 00:05:21,581
To go out and breathe fresh air,
swim in the ocean...

27
00:05:21,687 --> 00:05:25,648
I can't believe I won.
You call me Mr. Popular, I know.

28
00:05:25,751 --> 00:05:28,303
It's me. It's me.

29
00:05:28,374 --> 00:05:32,814
You guys know I'm not like this,
but this is just amazing.

30
00:05:33,622 --> 00:05:36,207
I'm going to the Island!
We're gonna have so much fun!

31
00:05:36,278 --> 00:05:40,053
But I need to see you guys out there.
You can do it! I won!

32
00:05:40,118 --> 00:05:41,362
That was this week's...

33
00:05:41,430 --> 00:05:43,885
We got a disturbance
on elevator 12, plaza level.

34
00:05:43,958 --> 00:05:47,536
...just moments before his
final departure to the Island,

35
00:05:47,606 --> 00:05:50,540
nature's last remaining
pathogen-free zone.

36
00:05:50,613 --> 00:05:52,752
- Lucky guy, huh?
- You can be a winner too.

37
00:05:52,853 --> 00:05:55,788
The next lottery is tonight.

38
00:05:57,077 --> 00:06:00,589
The next lottery is tonight.

39
00:06:02,772 --> 00:06:05,521
- How long have you been here?
- Two years.

40
00:06:06,709 --> 00:06:09,010
- What about you?
- Three.

41
00:06:09,076 --> 00:06:10,986
Three. I've been here seven.

42
00:06:11,059 --> 00:06:15,150
If I do the math, that makes me
the biggest lottery loser in the room.

43
00:06:16,627 --> 00:06:19,245
I'm such a loser.

44
00:06:47,793 --> 00:06:50,030
Sir.

45
00:06:50,098 --> 00:06:52,007
Yeah, you.

46
00:06:53,937 --> 00:06:55,431
Swipe.

47
00:06:56,880 --> 00:07:00,263
Gandu Three Echo, you've been flagged
for public disturbance before.

48
00:07:00,368 --> 00:07:03,216
Yes, I had a very small
emotional outburst, sir.

49
00:07:03,281 --> 00:07:05,768
- Safe to say it's over?
- Yes, very safe.

50
00:07:06,640 --> 00:07:09,706
- I'm feeling much better.
- Well, then, have a pleasant day.

51
00:07:09,776 --> 00:07:12,525
Thank you, you too.
You both have a pleasant day too.

52
00:07:34,543 --> 00:07:35,949
Feel the stretch.

53
00:07:37,550 --> 00:07:38,794
One more breath in.

54
00:07:54,670 --> 00:07:56,360
But I was in that section.

55
00:07:56,429 --> 00:07:57,956
No, I don't understand!

56
00:07:58,029 --> 00:08:00,549
- I tried! I tried to do the best I...
- Listen to me!

57
00:08:01,548 --> 00:08:06,283
Remember, be polite,
pleasant and peaceful.

58
00:08:06,381 --> 00:08:10,025
A healthy person is a happy person.

59
00:08:16,492 --> 00:08:20,234
Lincoln Six Echo, choices are fruit,
oatmeal and any type of bran.

60
00:08:20,299 --> 00:08:21,728
No bacon today?

61
00:08:21,804 --> 00:08:23,909
You got a nutrition flag,
means no bacon.

62
00:08:23,980 --> 00:08:26,401
In that case, two eggs,
over easy, not too runny,

63
00:08:26,475 --> 00:08:27,849
and a side of sausages.

64
00:08:27,915 --> 00:08:30,632
Maybe some French toast
and a little powdered sugar.

65
00:08:31,371 --> 00:08:34,949
You ain't cute and I got no time
for your lip, Six Echo.

66
00:08:35,050 --> 00:08:36,872
Now, what's it gonna be?

67
00:08:36,939 --> 00:08:37,953
Move it.

68
00:08:40,714 --> 00:08:41,958
Surprise me.

69
00:08:47,434 --> 00:08:48,448
Surprise.

70
00:08:49,994 --> 00:08:52,547
Yummy. Next.

71
00:09:03,881 --> 00:09:06,532
Watch and learn.

72
00:09:07,432 --> 00:09:09,025
Next.

73
00:09:09,129 --> 00:09:11,463
Jordan Two Delta.

74
00:09:11,528 --> 00:09:13,022
- Hi, honey.
- Hi.

75
00:09:13,128 --> 00:09:16,477
Choices are powdered eggs,
dried fruit and yogurt.

76
00:09:16,552 --> 00:09:19,301
- Eggs, please.
- OK.

77
00:09:20,936 --> 00:09:23,586
So, where were you the other day?
We missed you.

78
00:09:24,263 --> 00:09:27,198
That's nice of you to say, sweetheart.

79
00:09:27,847 --> 00:09:29,407
Get you anything else?

80
00:09:30,375 --> 00:09:31,585
Maybe a little bacon.

81
00:09:32,199 --> 00:09:34,141
No, it says I shouldn't.

82
00:09:34,215 --> 00:09:37,792
- Go ahead.
- Four, five pieces, please.

83
00:09:39,462 --> 00:09:40,706
Thank you.

84
00:09:42,406 --> 00:09:44,315
Well, good luck.
Gotta run along now.

85
00:09:44,422 --> 00:09:47,520
You're not going.
You gotta stay for dinner.

86
00:09:47,590 --> 00:09:50,143
- I softened her up for you.
- No doubt.

87
00:09:50,214 --> 00:09:52,800
- Back on your diet?
- You kidding? I love this stuff.

88
00:09:52,870 --> 00:09:55,520
Better eat up.
You'll need all your strength tonight.

89
00:09:55,589 --> 00:09:56,734
Is that a challenge?

90
00:09:56,805 --> 00:09:59,325
I promise I'll go easy on you.

91
00:10:01,669 --> 00:10:04,898
Please separate.
Find your seats now.

92
00:10:04,965 --> 00:10:06,820
Yeah.

93
00:10:07,653 --> 00:10:12,290
"'Who wants Sally? ' said Dick.
'I do,' said Jane.

94
00:10:12,356 --> 00:10:15,039
'I cannot find Sally.

95
00:10:15,108 --> 00:10:19,615
Get up, Dick.
Get up and help me find Sally.

96
00:10:19,684 --> 00:10:22,171
Is Sally here?"'

97
00:10:33,923 --> 00:10:36,542
Dr. Merrick will see you now.

98
00:10:40,802 --> 00:10:43,519
What'd you do wrong this time,
tough guy?

99
00:10:46,786 --> 00:10:48,957
Sir?

100
00:10:49,026 --> 00:10:53,631
- You wanted to see me?
- Yes. Please.

101
00:11:01,441 --> 00:11:03,808
Please, sit down.

102
00:11:04,577 --> 00:11:07,130
So, how is Lincoln Six Echo today?

103
00:11:07,201 --> 00:11:09,656
Not so good, I guess.

104
00:11:09,729 --> 00:11:11,638
Why do you say that?

105
00:11:11,713 --> 00:11:14,396
Well, if I'm here,
it means I'm not so good.

106
00:11:14,496 --> 00:11:17,365
That's a rather negative association.

107
00:11:17,473 --> 00:11:21,695
My only job is to see that you're happy,
things are OK with you.

108
00:11:21,760 --> 00:11:23,287
Right.

109
00:11:26,368 --> 00:11:29,303
Your file shows that you've
been interacting regularly

110
00:11:29,376 --> 00:11:30,619
with Jordan Two Delta.

111
00:11:30,687 --> 00:11:34,462
- There's no law against friendship.
- No. No, we encourage it,

112
00:11:34,527 --> 00:11:38,750
but, obviously,
proximity could become a concern.

113
00:11:38,815 --> 00:11:40,702
I know the rules of proximity.

114
00:11:42,942 --> 00:11:45,495
You've been doing quite well
in most other areas.

115
00:11:45,599 --> 00:11:48,468
Proficient at work,
exercising rigorously.

116
00:11:48,574 --> 00:11:51,957
But screening has picked up
some trace levels,

117
00:11:52,062 --> 00:11:55,990
changes in your metabolism,
and you've been having nightmares.

118
00:11:56,062 --> 00:11:58,745
Are you saying there's
something wrong with me?

119
00:11:58,813 --> 00:12:01,301
Why don't you tell me
about your dream?

120
00:12:01,982 --> 00:12:06,204
Well, it's the same dream every time.
I'm on a boat, headed to the Island.

121
00:12:06,269 --> 00:12:09,400
A boat? What kind of boat?

122
00:12:10,877 --> 00:12:12,154
A nice boat.

123
00:12:12,221 --> 00:12:13,715
Draw it for me, would you?

124
00:12:19,005 --> 00:12:22,300
So, you are heading
toward the Island.

125
00:12:22,364 --> 00:12:24,273
What happens then?

126
00:12:24,380 --> 00:12:27,097
- I drown.
- Really?

127
00:12:28,028 --> 00:12:30,962
- Why do you think that is?
- I don't know. You tell me.

128
00:12:31,036 --> 00:12:33,938
- Maybe you're afraid of winning.
- Why would I be afraid?

129
00:12:34,012 --> 00:12:35,800
You tell me.

130
00:12:40,347 --> 00:12:42,616
What's troubling you, Lincoln?

131
00:12:44,730 --> 00:12:46,519
Well, it's...

132
00:12:46,587 --> 00:12:48,659
It's just...

133
00:12:49,434 --> 00:12:51,605
All right.
Tuesday night is tofu night.

134
00:12:51,706 --> 00:12:54,870
And I'm asking myself, who decided
that everyone here likes tofu

135
00:12:54,938 --> 00:12:57,425
in the first place?
And what is tofu, anyway?

136
00:12:57,498 --> 00:13:00,564
And why can't I have bacon?
I line up every morning,

137
00:13:00,634 --> 00:13:03,449
and I'm not allowed any bacon
for my breakfast.

138
00:13:03,514 --> 00:13:05,586
And...
Let's talk about all the white.

139
00:13:05,657 --> 00:13:07,762
Why is everyone
wearing white all the time?

140
00:13:07,833 --> 00:13:11,346
It's impossible to keep clean.
I always get the gray stripe.

141
00:13:11,417 --> 00:13:14,002
I never get any color.
And I hand it in to be cleaned,

142
00:13:14,073 --> 00:13:17,968
and someone cleans it, and folds it
neatly back in my drawer, but who?

143
00:13:18,040 --> 00:13:20,790
Who is that person? I don't know.

144
00:13:20,889 --> 00:13:22,514
I just... I wanna know answers.

145
00:13:22,617 --> 00:13:25,235
And I wish that there was more.

146
00:13:26,392 --> 00:13:28,181
- More?
- Yeah.

147
00:13:28,248 --> 00:13:32,371
More than just waiting
to go to the Island.

148
00:13:35,063 --> 00:13:37,300
Lincoln,

149
00:13:37,368 --> 00:13:40,084
it's your nature
to question things.

150
00:13:40,152 --> 00:13:44,821
But don't you realize how lucky you are?
That you survived the contamination.

151
00:13:44,887 --> 00:13:48,913
That nature has left you
a Garden of Eden to repopulate.

152
00:13:48,983 --> 00:13:52,081
That, Lincoln, is your purpose.

153
00:13:55,798 --> 00:13:59,595
Right. And you?
Aren't you going to the Island too?

154
00:13:59,702 --> 00:14:02,004
No.

155
00:14:02,070 --> 00:14:05,168
My responsibility is to make sure

156
00:14:05,238 --> 00:14:07,441
this facility continues to operate.

157
00:14:07,509 --> 00:14:12,910
That's why people like me,
my staff and supervisors, we...

158
00:14:12,981 --> 00:14:15,534
...we can't win the lottery.

159
00:14:18,452 --> 00:14:20,208
Let me see that.

160
00:14:22,229 --> 00:14:23,985
You draw well.

161
00:14:24,053 --> 00:14:26,900
"Renovatio."
What does that mean?

162
00:14:26,964 --> 00:14:29,135
I don't know.
It's always in my dream.

163
00:14:31,380 --> 00:14:33,747
I'd like to run some tests
on you, Lincoln.

164
00:14:34,516 --> 00:14:35,890
What sort of tests?

165
00:14:36,724 --> 00:14:39,179
Nice tests.

166
00:14:39,252 --> 00:14:40,528
Come with me.

167
00:14:47,347 --> 00:14:49,038
Take a seat.

168
00:14:53,842 --> 00:14:55,850
OK, let's get you comfortable.

169
00:14:55,922 --> 00:14:57,351
Swing back.

170
00:15:01,906 --> 00:15:05,201
- I thought these were nice tests.
- It's a synaptic brain scan.

171
00:15:05,266 --> 00:15:07,371
Totally harmless.

172
00:15:07,442 --> 00:15:10,289
Don't worry, it's painless.

173
00:15:30,384 --> 00:15:31,846
- It hurts.
- Not really.

174
00:15:31,952 --> 00:15:33,578
- Yeah, it does!
- No, it doesn't.

175
00:15:33,679 --> 00:15:35,883
Yeah, it really, really does!

176
00:15:40,815 --> 00:15:43,881
The micro-sensors
will move along your optic nerve.

177
00:15:43,951 --> 00:15:47,147
They'll be uploading readings
to us over the next 24 hours,

178
00:15:47,215 --> 00:15:49,801
after which,
you'll pass them through your urine.

179
00:15:49,871 --> 00:15:51,911
Now, that might hurt.

180
00:16:02,798 --> 00:16:04,391
Six Echo, you're late.

181
00:16:18,637 --> 00:16:20,547
Jones, you ever get bored doing this?

182
00:16:20,621 --> 00:16:21,798
- Doing what?
- This.

183
00:16:21,869 --> 00:16:24,738
- I never really thought about it.
- I think about it a lot.

184
00:16:24,812 --> 00:16:26,700
- About what?
- This boring job.

185
00:16:26,765 --> 00:16:29,798
- What are we doing here?
- We're feeding the nutrient lines.

186
00:16:29,868 --> 00:16:33,348
We eat food, food's gotta have
vitamins, right? It's good for us.

187
00:16:33,452 --> 00:16:35,972
You don't ever wonder about anything?

188
00:16:36,075 --> 00:16:38,442
Where do these tubes go?

189
00:16:39,628 --> 00:16:41,002
They start there.

190
00:16:41,068 --> 00:16:43,883
And they go... right there.

191
00:16:45,068 --> 00:16:47,850
Hey. Did you get a look
at the new guy?

192
00:16:47,915 --> 00:16:49,890
Seven Foxtrot.

193
00:16:49,963 --> 00:16:53,575
They found another survivor.
They keep finding them.

194
00:16:53,643 --> 00:16:55,236
He'll probably win the lottery.

195
00:16:55,307 --> 00:16:58,438
Straight down, in the hole.
There you go, you try it.

196
00:16:58,507 --> 00:17:01,671
Straight down in the hole.

197
00:17:01,739 --> 00:17:05,415
In the hole.
No, no, no. Put it down.

198
00:17:05,514 --> 00:17:08,776
Did we all look that stupid
when we went through decontamination?

199
00:17:08,842 --> 00:17:13,184
Hey, Mr. Man-With-All-The-Questions,
let me ask you this:

200
00:17:13,962 --> 00:17:16,067
Lottery's supposed
to be random, right?

201
00:17:16,138 --> 00:17:17,185
Right.

202
00:17:17,257 --> 00:17:19,493
What if it's not?
What if it's rigged?

203
00:17:20,201 --> 00:17:21,313
Rigged?

204
00:17:22,729 --> 00:17:24,736
I've been working on this. Here.

205
00:17:24,809 --> 00:17:26,718
Take a look at that.

206
00:17:27,368 --> 00:17:30,270
It charts the last 20 people
that won a spot on the Island.

207
00:17:30,344 --> 00:17:33,508
Excluding, of course, the women,
picked to be breeders.

208
00:17:33,576 --> 00:17:36,390
- What is this?
- I took the first letter in each name.

209
00:17:36,488 --> 00:17:39,455
I assigned it a point value system,
based on the alphabet,

210
00:17:39,560 --> 00:17:41,894
like the last guy,
Starkweather, S equals 15.

211
00:17:41,959 --> 00:17:43,552
Q equals 15, S equals 19.

212
00:17:43,624 --> 00:17:45,631
- Do you see what I'm saying?
- No.

213
00:17:45,703 --> 00:17:49,052
Well, maybe if you would listen to me,
I'm trying to tell you.

214
00:17:49,128 --> 00:17:52,389
You string the numbers together.
You divide it by the amount...

215
00:17:52,455 --> 00:17:55,717
You multiply... You divide it by
the amount of... You divide it...

216
00:17:55,783 --> 00:18:00,093
You divide it by the amount of people,
which is 25, a thousand plus five, 2500.

217
00:18:00,166 --> 00:18:03,778
You know what that spells?
J-O-N-E-S.

218
00:18:04,710 --> 00:18:07,328
- I'm winning the lottery tonight.
- Did you pack?

219
00:18:08,710 --> 00:18:10,117
- No.
- Gentlemen,

220
00:18:11,013 --> 00:18:13,468
I'm gonna go mess with Foxtrot.

221
00:18:13,574 --> 00:18:15,581
There you go. Straight.

222
00:18:15,686 --> 00:18:17,857
Straight down in the hole.

223
00:18:17,926 --> 00:18:19,714
- There you go.
- Straight...

224
00:18:21,605 --> 00:18:23,710
- What? He had something on his... OK.
- Go.

225
00:18:28,837 --> 00:18:30,528
Lima! Are you OK?
What's wrong?

226
00:18:30,597 --> 00:18:34,077
Code 15, we need med-techs stat!
Lima One Alpha.

227
00:18:34,148 --> 00:18:35,806
Let's give her some air, OK?

228
00:18:35,876 --> 00:18:38,396
You're gonna be OK, all right?
Relax and breathe.

229
00:18:38,468 --> 00:18:40,988
Can I get a wheelchair?
It's for Lima One Alpha.

230
00:18:41,092 --> 00:18:44,408
- You OK?
- I think it's time.

231
00:18:46,404 --> 00:18:49,720
Lima, you're going to the Island.

232
00:18:49,827 --> 00:18:52,674
- We're going.
- Oh, you're so lucky.

233
00:18:52,740 --> 00:18:54,562
I hope I see you soon.

234
00:18:57,123 --> 00:19:01,792
Everyone, please follow her out.
Quickly and carefully. Watch the glass.

235
00:19:01,859 --> 00:19:03,898
- Good luck, Lima.
- Thank you.

236
00:19:08,099 --> 00:19:10,433
That's fair. That's real fair.

237
00:19:10,498 --> 00:19:13,814
Ladies, ladies, push back, please.
Gentlemen. Thank you.

238
00:19:17,474 --> 00:19:19,710
Everyone, back to work.

239
00:19:19,777 --> 00:19:21,664
That is so not fair.

240
00:19:22,369 --> 00:19:26,362
Oh, man, I hate this jealousy thing.
It's giving me heart palpitations.

241
00:19:26,433 --> 00:19:28,408
Tech Services.

242
00:19:28,481 --> 00:19:30,204
Computer's down again.

243
00:19:31,073 --> 00:19:33,015
I'm down.
Computer guy's in Sector Six.

244
00:19:33,089 --> 00:19:36,350
I have to deal with this mess.
Take my Tri-Key. Contamination kit.

245
00:19:36,416 --> 00:19:38,424
- Hurry back.
- Absolutely.

246
00:20:05,854 --> 00:20:08,723
- Hey! What are you doing?
- I'm gonna see this guy.

247
00:20:09,887 --> 00:20:13,563
Hey, chief. We got live wires
all over the place here.

248
00:20:13,630 --> 00:20:16,728
Hey, I've been looking all over for you.

249
00:20:17,373 --> 00:20:18,900
- What?
- I've been looking...

250
00:20:19,006 --> 00:20:21,788
- Can't hear you.
- I've been looking all over for you.

251
00:20:21,854 --> 00:20:26,076
If you go and get yourself contaminated,
don't come pointing the finger at me.

252
00:20:26,141 --> 00:20:27,352
How you doing, Mac?

253
00:20:27,997 --> 00:20:30,517
- What are you doing here?
- My chip fried again.

254
00:20:30,589 --> 00:20:33,404
Yeah. How much longer
do you think that one's gonna work?

255
00:20:35,612 --> 00:20:38,579
- What are you two clowns looking at?
- Hey,

256
00:20:38,652 --> 00:20:40,627
you got any of that stuff
on you today?

257
00:20:41,309 --> 00:20:43,927
Oh, look, it's break time.
Come on.

258
00:20:45,468 --> 00:20:48,315
You're a bad influence on me.

259
00:20:48,380 --> 00:20:51,195
Must be why I like you so much.

260
00:20:54,619 --> 00:20:57,968
What's it like where you live?
In Sector Five?

261
00:20:59,003 --> 00:21:02,483
It's fine. You know,
it's like any other sector, I guess.

262
00:21:05,691 --> 00:21:08,560
I like coming out here, talking.

263
00:21:08,635 --> 00:21:11,188
Most supervisors don't like to talk.

264
00:21:11,259 --> 00:21:12,338
Yeah.

265
00:21:13,914 --> 00:21:15,823
Step into my office.

266
00:21:21,978 --> 00:21:24,825
- Are these your friends?
- Yeah, sometimes.

267
00:21:24,889 --> 00:21:26,744
Where are their clothes?

268
00:21:26,809 --> 00:21:28,053
What's with Dr. Merrick?

269
00:21:28,121 --> 00:21:32,594
You mean why does he act like he's
got a filing cabinet shoved up his ass?

270
00:21:32,665 --> 00:21:33,712
Yeah.

271
00:21:33,785 --> 00:21:35,989
It's called a God complex.

272
00:21:36,057 --> 00:21:38,991
All doctors are like that.
They think they know everything.

273
00:21:39,064 --> 00:21:41,104
What's God?

274
00:21:41,177 --> 00:21:43,632
Well, you know when you
want something really bad

275
00:21:43,705 --> 00:21:45,810
and you close your eyes
and you wish for it?

276
00:21:45,881 --> 00:21:49,939
- God's the guy that ignores you.
- Oh. Right.

277
00:21:50,008 --> 00:21:52,561
Tech Service requested
in Product Extraction.

278
00:21:52,663 --> 00:21:54,736
Yeah, I'll be right there.

279
00:21:58,071 --> 00:22:00,820
Oh, hey. Let me get that.

280
00:22:00,888 --> 00:22:03,670
Where do you get that stuff, anyway?

281
00:22:03,735 --> 00:22:06,418
It's an old stash.
You know, from before.

282
00:22:06,487 --> 00:22:08,494
You mean from
before the contamination?

283
00:22:08,567 --> 00:22:11,666
Yeah. Come on, you're killing me
with questions here.

284
00:22:11,735 --> 00:22:13,491
You got a sweet deal here, you know?

285
00:22:13,559 --> 00:22:16,788
Because you're,
you know, like, special.

286
00:22:16,854 --> 00:22:18,577
Why? Why am I special?

287
00:22:18,646 --> 00:22:20,206
There's another question.

288
00:22:21,270 --> 00:22:23,058
You remember what we talked about?

289
00:22:23,125 --> 00:22:25,580
You don't tell anybody
about our conversations?

290
00:22:25,686 --> 00:22:28,784
- 'Cause that can get me in big trouble.
- No, I don't.

291
00:22:28,885 --> 00:22:30,292
Good.

292
00:23:06,227 --> 00:23:07,950
How's it going?

293
00:23:10,355 --> 00:23:13,388
Hey, how are you?
How's your world?

294
00:23:14,066 --> 00:23:16,106
OK, I'll catch you later.

295
00:23:19,986 --> 00:23:21,928
Chinese junk locked up again, huh?

296
00:23:22,002 --> 00:23:23,344
Yep.

297
00:23:23,410 --> 00:23:25,264
What a surprise.

298
00:23:27,601 --> 00:23:28,943
Go hot.

299
00:23:33,073 --> 00:23:35,921
- You better fix that thing.
- Yeah.

300
00:23:36,497 --> 00:23:38,831
You'd think with the money
this place rakes in

301
00:23:38,897 --> 00:23:41,264
- they could afford decent equipment.
- Yeah.

302
00:23:42,609 --> 00:23:43,819
Ready?

303
00:23:45,776 --> 00:23:47,238
Cut the O2.

304
00:23:49,232 --> 00:23:53,007
Seriously, unless you want to see me
blow chunks, can you wait till I'm gone?

305
00:23:53,072 --> 00:23:55,079
- Sever the umbilical.
- Cutting.

306
00:24:17,006 --> 00:24:18,697
Breathe.

307
00:24:20,238 --> 00:24:22,147
Come on, yeah. That's it.

308
00:24:25,358 --> 00:24:27,878
Come on, breathe. Breathe.

309
00:24:27,950 --> 00:24:29,128
Come on.

310
00:24:30,253 --> 00:24:32,937
Come on, come on!
Breathe, breathe!

311
00:24:33,037 --> 00:24:35,306
There we go.
Now we're working.

312
00:24:35,373 --> 00:24:37,129
He's healthy.

313
00:24:39,053 --> 00:24:40,679
Welcome to the world.

314
00:24:44,236 --> 00:24:46,244
So, how's Three Helo?

315
00:24:46,316 --> 00:24:47,723
Good.

316
00:24:49,773 --> 00:24:51,528
He's feisty. Light.

317
00:24:53,260 --> 00:24:55,911
Vitals seem fine.

318
00:24:56,748 --> 00:24:59,563
- Smooth extraction?
- Yep.

319
00:25:01,900 --> 00:25:04,485
Looks like we have a fine product.

320
00:25:04,588 --> 00:25:06,726
Tag him and ship him to Foundation.

321
00:26:20,742 --> 00:26:22,400
Little bug.

322
00:27:07,683 --> 00:27:10,717
Maybe next time I won't embarrass you
in front of your friends.

323
00:27:17,987 --> 00:27:19,929
It was very sad.

324
00:27:20,515 --> 00:27:21,725
- Hey.
- Hello.

325
00:27:21,795 --> 00:27:23,518
Hi.

326
00:27:24,866 --> 00:27:27,714
So you just let
a little girl beat you, huh?

327
00:27:29,283 --> 00:27:30,941
Stim units restricted.

328
00:27:31,010 --> 00:27:32,952
Yeah, yeah.
I'll have the veggie stuff.

329
00:27:33,026 --> 00:27:35,743
Papassian petal juice, please.

330
00:27:35,809 --> 00:27:37,435
It's good for the skin.

331
00:27:49,217 --> 00:27:50,624
Jordan, are you sick?

332
00:27:52,032 --> 00:27:56,309
When I was in Dr. Merrick's office,
I thought I saw your name on a file.

333
00:27:56,384 --> 00:27:58,010
No, I'm fine.

334
00:27:58,720 --> 00:28:00,247
OK.

335
00:28:00,865 --> 00:28:02,687
How are you?

336
00:28:02,752 --> 00:28:04,759
I'm fine.

337
00:28:04,832 --> 00:28:06,654
Lincoln, I can tell when you're lying

338
00:28:06,720 --> 00:28:09,851
'cause your mouth smiles
but your eyes don't.

339
00:28:12,255 --> 00:28:13,270
I found something.

340
00:28:13,344 --> 00:28:14,554
- What?
- A bug.

341
00:28:15,135 --> 00:28:16,793
- A bug?
- A flying bug.

342
00:28:16,895 --> 00:28:17,822
Can I see it?

343
00:28:17,919 --> 00:28:19,959
I think it came
in the ventilation shaft.

344
00:28:20,063 --> 00:28:22,649
I thought they went extinct
with the contamination.

345
00:28:22,719 --> 00:28:25,174
I know. And how did it get by
the pathogen sensors?

346
00:28:25,247 --> 00:28:27,734
- It must be too small.
- No, it's not too small.

347
00:28:27,806 --> 00:28:30,937
How did it survive out there, anyway?
How does anyone survive?

348
00:28:31,006 --> 00:28:33,756
They keep finding people,
but where do they come from?

349
00:28:33,822 --> 00:28:36,822
It's good that they find survivors.

350
00:28:36,893 --> 00:28:40,570
Why do you always question the good?
You only think about the bad.

351
00:28:40,637 --> 00:28:43,158
I just have a feeling
that something is wrong.

352
00:28:44,094 --> 00:28:46,362
Good things do happen.

353
00:28:46,430 --> 00:28:48,601
I want to see that bug.

354
00:28:50,045 --> 00:28:52,914
Hey. Gandu learned a new word
from the censor.

355
00:28:53,021 --> 00:28:55,060
- What?
- "Dude."

356
00:28:55,165 --> 00:28:56,507
"Dude"?

357
00:28:56,573 --> 00:28:58,744
- What does it mean?
- He just called me dude.

358
00:28:58,813 --> 00:29:00,820
- Hey, dude.
- He said "Hey, dude"?

359
00:29:00,892 --> 00:29:02,714
- D-O-O-D. "Dude."
- Hey, dude.

360
00:29:02,780 --> 00:29:04,438
- Dude.
- Dude.

361
00:29:04,508 --> 00:29:06,963
- Lottery's gonna start.
- Like you stand a chance.

362
00:29:07,036 --> 00:29:07,985
Dude.

363
00:29:09,020 --> 00:29:11,671
Light up all etherscreens.

364
00:29:11,740 --> 00:29:14,871
And... start the lottery.

365
00:29:22,363 --> 00:29:23,540
Good evening.

366
00:29:23,643 --> 00:29:27,636
Live from Ether-Con,
welcome to the lottery spin.

367
00:29:28,603 --> 00:29:30,457
It's been a busy week.

368
00:29:30,523 --> 00:29:33,457
We've had a record two winners so far.

369
00:29:33,530 --> 00:29:36,661
Tonight's winner will be selected
at random for relocation

370
00:29:36,730 --> 00:29:40,886
to the Island, transported
to the world's last paradise.

371
00:29:40,953 --> 00:29:44,117
- And start the spin.
- And now, let the spin begin.

372
00:29:49,145 --> 00:29:52,243
Jordan Two Delta, step up.

373
00:29:52,345 --> 00:29:57,047
Your time has come.
You're moving out to the Island.

374
00:30:02,296 --> 00:30:06,093
For everyone else, never lose hope.

375
00:30:08,664 --> 00:30:10,486
Thank you. Thank you.

376
00:30:10,552 --> 00:30:13,203
I can't believe it.

377
00:30:20,695 --> 00:30:23,030
I have to go in the morning.

378
00:30:23,095 --> 00:30:25,004
You were right.

379
00:30:26,519 --> 00:30:29,039
Good things do happen.

380
00:30:32,823 --> 00:30:35,539
I wish I'd known you better.

381
00:30:36,727 --> 00:30:38,319
You two.

382
00:30:38,390 --> 00:30:39,765
Watch your proximity.

383
00:30:48,149 --> 00:30:50,320
I'll see you on the Island.

384
00:31:07,541 --> 00:31:10,889
You want to go to the Island.

385
00:31:15,700 --> 00:31:16,976
Breathe!

386
00:31:18,388 --> 00:31:19,882
You've been chosen.

387
00:31:21,907 --> 00:31:24,874
The Island awaits you.

388
00:32:39,854 --> 00:32:43,683
Check into the nurses' station
up the corridor, take your first left.

389
00:32:44,974 --> 00:32:47,494
Dr. Lemon, call 915.

390
00:32:47,566 --> 00:32:49,705
Dr. Lemon, call 915.

391
00:33:49,994 --> 00:33:52,132
She's so beautiful.

392
00:33:53,450 --> 00:33:55,392
I've never seen a baby.

393
00:33:55,466 --> 00:33:56,775
Can I hold her?

394
00:33:56,842 --> 00:33:58,303
Notjust yet.

395
00:34:04,425 --> 00:34:06,792
Are we going to the Island?

396
00:35:21,284 --> 00:35:23,193
Oh, my God.

397
00:35:23,748 --> 00:35:26,052
Congratulations, it's a beautiful girl.

398
00:35:26,052 --> 00:35:27,840
- Oh, my gosh.
- Thank you.

399
00:35:27,907 --> 00:35:29,795
It's my baby. Oh, my gosh.

400
00:35:29,860 --> 00:35:31,070
Whenever you're ready,

401
00:35:31,139 --> 00:35:34,717
we have copies of your
policy termination for your records.

402
00:35:34,787 --> 00:35:37,405
Look at her. She's beautiful.

403
00:35:39,651 --> 00:35:43,295
Starkweather? That big, cute football
player on the Reebok commercials?

404
00:35:43,362 --> 00:35:46,013
I love him! Is he in there?
I thought that was him, girl!

405
00:35:46,115 --> 00:35:47,675
I just love him!

406
00:35:48,355 --> 00:35:50,744
That's great.
Listen, you're a real hoot.

407
00:35:50,850 --> 00:35:52,705
Any chance I can make this pickup?

408
00:35:52,770 --> 00:35:54,974
Well, he's still in surgery. Sorry.

409
00:35:55,042 --> 00:35:59,165
Lady, I've got a bird on the pad
and a storm's coming in.

410
00:35:59,233 --> 00:36:02,397
We don't fly in bad weather.

411
00:36:05,825 --> 00:36:08,411
They look real busy.
So I'd have a seat.

412
00:36:09,409 --> 00:36:11,798
Grim Reaper coming in here
with an attitude.

413
00:36:11,873 --> 00:36:16,793
Heart rate 102.
BP 126 over 82.

414
00:36:16,897 --> 00:36:18,806
- Laser cutter ready?
- It's ready.

415
00:36:18,913 --> 00:36:21,760
- Make sure suction's functioning.
- Ventilating easily.

416
00:36:21,856 --> 00:36:23,678
- Very good.
- Grid in place.

417
00:36:23,744 --> 00:36:24,889
Prepare that bone saw.

418
00:36:26,816 --> 00:36:29,303
I think we're about ready to open.

419
00:36:47,039 --> 00:36:48,249
Let's clean that drip.

420
00:36:52,798 --> 00:36:54,653
Doctor, heart rate's rising.

421
00:36:56,478 --> 00:37:00,700
Heart rate's still rising, doctor.

422
00:37:03,965 --> 00:37:06,780
- What's his blood pressure?
- BP 138 over 92.

423
00:37:09,053 --> 00:37:10,940
Heart rate's still rising.

424
00:37:11,005 --> 00:37:14,071
- Boost the anesthetic level!
- He's fighting the ventilator.

425
00:37:14,141 --> 00:37:16,563
I don't wanna euthanize this guy
to get his liver!

426
00:37:24,764 --> 00:37:25,876
Guards!

427
00:37:27,324 --> 00:37:29,146
Oh, my God!

428
00:37:36,091 --> 00:37:38,841
Stop that man! Get him!

429
00:37:45,114 --> 00:37:47,089
Stop!

430
00:38:03,001 --> 00:38:05,008
All right, relax, relax, big guy.
Relax.

431
00:38:05,081 --> 00:38:07,088
Easy, easy, easy!
Don't damage him!

432
00:38:10,522 --> 00:38:11,983
- Relax!
- No!

433
00:38:12,057 --> 00:38:14,478
I don't want to die, no! No!

434
00:38:14,553 --> 00:38:18,262
I want to go to the Island!
You promised!

435
00:38:18,329 --> 00:38:21,624
I wanna live!
I don't wanna die!

436
00:38:21,689 --> 00:38:23,216
No!

437
00:38:25,432 --> 00:38:26,839
Hey.

438
00:38:27,576 --> 00:38:30,991
You OK, buddy? It's not the first time
this has happened, you know.

439
00:38:31,096 --> 00:38:34,063
Ether-Con. Product is secure.

440
00:38:44,951 --> 00:38:46,609
Check this part out.

441
00:38:46,679 --> 00:38:48,621
Wait, OK, watch.
Wait, wait.

442
00:38:48,695 --> 00:38:52,273
Boom! Did you see that? Man.

443
00:38:52,343 --> 00:38:54,798
That is so cruel, man.

444
00:38:55,543 --> 00:38:58,161
Oh, man. Down for the count.

445
00:38:58,262 --> 00:39:02,419
Gentlemen, I understand
there's been an incident.

446
00:39:02,486 --> 00:39:05,355
Sir, Starkweather ran
from the operating theater.

447
00:39:05,462 --> 00:39:07,916
- And do you find that funny?
- No, sir.

448
00:39:07,989 --> 00:39:10,956
- Do you?
- Definitely not, sir.

449
00:39:11,029 --> 00:39:13,134
Play it back, please.

450
00:39:17,941 --> 00:39:19,729
Stop.

451
00:39:19,796 --> 00:39:21,422
- Who is that?
- That's just an RN.

452
00:39:21,493 --> 00:39:23,697
He was scared, I helped him up.

453
00:39:24,629 --> 00:39:26,058
Play it back at half-speed.

454
00:39:32,596 --> 00:39:34,189
Freeze.

455
00:39:35,348 --> 00:39:36,657
Magnify his wrist.

456
00:39:41,364 --> 00:39:43,152
We have a product on the loose.

457
00:39:44,340 --> 00:39:46,674
- Get me a facial match.
- We're on it.

458
00:39:46,739 --> 00:39:49,160
- Let's go.
- OK, down to Level 2.

459
00:40:01,362 --> 00:40:03,533
You can't come in here!

460
00:40:08,626 --> 00:40:11,495
- Wait.
- Oh, my God.

461
00:40:28,241 --> 00:40:30,150
- How sweet.
- You gotta come with me.

462
00:40:30,224 --> 00:40:31,172
What?

463
00:40:31,248 --> 00:40:33,353
Move! Move!

464
00:40:41,551 --> 00:40:44,398
We got a match!
Lincoln Six Echo.

465
00:40:44,464 --> 00:40:46,733
I want a full contamination lockdown.

466
00:40:46,799 --> 00:40:48,140
Find Six Echo.

467
00:40:50,575 --> 00:40:52,397
- Masks down.
- What the hell?!

468
00:40:52,463 --> 00:40:55,528
- I need to see all your faces.
- I don't care what he says, nurse,

469
00:40:55,598 --> 00:40:58,380
that's live human tissue.
Seal that liver now.

470
00:40:58,447 --> 00:41:00,072
Check the back corners!

471
00:41:04,078 --> 00:41:08,201
How did that agnate get upstairs
into the Medical Sector?

472
00:41:08,782 --> 00:41:10,308
Find out.

473
00:41:12,654 --> 00:41:15,174
- Men aren't supposed to be...
- You gotta trust me.

474
00:41:15,245 --> 00:41:16,193
- What?
- I saw them.

475
00:41:16,269 --> 00:41:18,473
- Who?
- Lima and Starkweather. They're dead.

476
00:41:18,541 --> 00:41:20,996
- What?
- They killed her and cut him open...

477
00:41:21,069 --> 00:41:22,956
Stop it!
I want to go back to my room.

478
00:41:23,020 --> 00:41:25,802
- They're gonna kill you.
- I'm going to the Island.

479
00:41:25,869 --> 00:41:27,941
Jordan, there is no Island!
Come on!

480
00:41:29,421 --> 00:41:32,039
I got Six Echo in Female Tower,
floor 32.

481
00:41:32,109 --> 00:41:34,727
- He's got a female product in tow.
- Track that.

482
00:41:34,796 --> 00:41:37,130
Get out of the way!

483
00:41:37,228 --> 00:41:38,918
Move! Move!

484
00:41:39,020 --> 00:41:41,027
Out of the way!
Get out. Now.

485
00:41:41,740 --> 00:41:42,885
Just trust me.

486
00:41:46,987 --> 00:41:49,354
This is a community bulletin.

487
00:41:49,419 --> 00:41:51,077
Attention, residents,

488
00:41:51,147 --> 00:41:55,075
a contamination alert
has been issued for Lincoln Six Echo.

489
00:41:55,147 --> 00:41:59,402
Anyone coming in contact with him
will be quarantined.

490
00:42:01,418 --> 00:42:03,839
Move! Move!

491
00:42:07,594 --> 00:42:09,187
Freeze! Stop right there!

492
00:42:29,193 --> 00:42:30,469
Go! Go! Go!

493
00:42:30,536 --> 00:42:31,584
Get out of the way!

494
00:42:40,296 --> 00:42:43,874
I've got two agnates on the move
on the second floor.

495
00:42:57,063 --> 00:42:59,037
There they are!

496
00:42:59,111 --> 00:43:03,486
I've got them in Sector Six basement!
Get them!

497
00:43:14,373 --> 00:43:16,195
- No!
- Stop!

498
00:43:26,405 --> 00:43:28,095
- Lincoln!
- Get up!

499
00:43:28,165 --> 00:43:29,147
No!

500
00:43:29,988 --> 00:43:31,549
Stop it!

501
00:43:33,253 --> 00:43:34,529
No!

502
00:44:10,722 --> 00:44:15,293
You've been chosen.
You have a very special purpose.

503
00:44:15,362 --> 00:44:18,842
You're part of a new beginning.
You're special.

504
00:44:18,945 --> 00:44:21,912
You have a very special purpose.

505
00:44:26,241 --> 00:44:29,088
You want to go to the Island.
Your purpose in life

506
00:44:29,153 --> 00:44:32,000
is to populate the Island.
You're part of a new beginning.

507
00:44:32,065 --> 00:44:35,709
You're special. Very special.
You've been chosen.

508
00:44:35,776 --> 00:44:38,646
You've been chosen.
Chosen to survive, to carry on.

509
00:44:38,720 --> 00:44:42,015
You want to go to the Island.

510
00:44:45,600 --> 00:44:49,212
- Go, go!
- You have a very special purpose.

511
00:44:52,832 --> 00:44:54,970
Very special.

512
00:44:56,064 --> 00:44:57,951
- He's gotta be in here.
- I'm looking!

513
00:44:58,015 --> 00:44:59,924
Check over here!

514
00:44:59,999 --> 00:45:01,308
Watch your left!

515
00:45:02,687 --> 00:45:03,832
Run!

516
00:45:06,654 --> 00:45:08,891
Go! Run!

517
00:45:08,959 --> 00:45:10,388
He's over here!

518
00:45:17,022 --> 00:45:19,094
There they are! Go!

519
00:45:32,349 --> 00:45:35,284
- Lincoln!
- Come on! Get him!

520
00:45:36,444 --> 00:45:38,899
- Let s go. Move!
- Come on!

521
00:45:41,212 --> 00:45:42,357
Come on! Come on!

522
00:45:42,428 --> 00:45:44,948
Damn! Go, go! Go!

523
00:45:45,020 --> 00:45:46,613
Come on, let's go!

524
00:45:49,948 --> 00:45:52,053
You still think there's an Island?

525
00:46:02,555 --> 00:46:03,864
Come on!

526
00:46:28,345 --> 00:46:30,647
Come on. Come on!

527
00:46:47,192 --> 00:46:49,613
There's a door over here!

528
00:48:02,131 --> 00:48:06,801
Lincoln Six Echo remains in quarantine
after contamination exposure.

529
00:48:06,867 --> 00:48:11,984
Jordan Two Delta was safely transported
to her new home on the Island.

530
00:48:12,051 --> 00:48:14,898
Jones Three Echo, I need you
to concentrate in this lab.

531
00:48:14,963 --> 00:48:18,508
Sir, I want to focus more than anything.
I love my job. It's interesting.

532
00:48:18,578 --> 00:48:21,578
But Lincoln Six Echo
has been contaminated,

533
00:48:21,651 --> 00:48:24,585
and it really worries me,
because he's a good friend of mine.

534
00:48:24,658 --> 00:48:27,025
He's one of my best friends.
My only best friend.

535
00:48:27,090 --> 00:48:29,130
He'll be fine, Three Echo.

536
00:48:29,202 --> 00:48:31,307
Sir, I have one question.

537
00:48:31,377 --> 00:48:33,417
Where do all the tubes go?

538
00:48:35,794 --> 00:48:37,616
The human organism.

539
00:48:37,681 --> 00:48:40,528
Unique in all the universe
in its complexity.

540
00:48:40,593 --> 00:48:43,408
The product of three billion years
of evolution.

541
00:48:43,473 --> 00:48:46,789
Perfect in every way, except one.

542
00:48:46,865 --> 00:48:49,254
Like all machines, it wears out.

543
00:48:50,897 --> 00:48:53,515
For centuries, the idea
of replenishing the human body

544
00:48:53,585 --> 00:48:55,624
has been
at the forefront of science.

545
00:48:55,696 --> 00:48:57,769
We need to turn this bad day
into a good day.

546
00:48:57,840 --> 00:48:59,595
- How?
- A terrific day. By selling.

547
00:48:59,664 --> 00:49:02,565
By selling. Sell, sell, sell.
You start, I finish.

548
00:49:12,430 --> 00:49:14,219
Ladies and gentlemen,

549
00:49:14,287 --> 00:49:18,062
welcome to
the next generation of science,

550
00:49:18,127 --> 00:49:20,014
the agnate.

551
00:49:20,078 --> 00:49:24,039
An organic frame engineered
directly into adulthood

552
00:49:24,110 --> 00:49:25,833
to match the client's age.

553
00:49:25,902 --> 00:49:28,324
- You're looking at stage one
- This way, sir.

554
00:49:28,397 --> 00:49:29,739
In its development.

555
00:49:29,806 --> 00:49:32,359
Within 12 months
it will be harvest-ready,

556
00:49:32,430 --> 00:49:35,943
providing a carrier for your baby,
a second pair of lungs, fresh skin.

557
00:49:36,014 --> 00:49:40,007
All genetically indistinguishable
from your own.

558
00:49:40,109 --> 00:49:44,681
And, in compliance with
the eugenics laws of 2015,

559
00:49:44,749 --> 00:49:49,702
all our agnates are maintained
in a persistent vegetative state.

560
00:49:49,772 --> 00:49:52,074
They never achieve consciousness.

561
00:49:52,141 --> 00:49:55,239
They never think or suffer

562
00:49:55,308 --> 00:49:59,170
or feel pain, joy, love, hate.

563
00:49:59,244 --> 00:50:01,961
It's a product, ladies and gentlemen,

564
00:50:02,028 --> 00:50:04,679
in every way that matters,

565
00:50:04,748 --> 00:50:07,431
not human.

566
00:50:11,499 --> 00:50:14,466
This is our public relations director,
Mr. Whitman.

567
00:50:14,571 --> 00:50:16,579
He'll be happy
to answer any questions.

568
00:50:16,683 --> 00:50:19,050
Once again, thank you.
Mr. Whitman.

569
00:50:19,147 --> 00:50:23,008
I want to talk about the smartest
investment you'll ever make.

570
00:50:23,594 --> 00:50:27,489
And I want to tell you how you're
gonna live 60 to 70 years longer.

571
00:50:31,370 --> 00:50:34,566
Dr. Merrick, Albert Laurent,
Blackhawk Security.

572
00:50:34,633 --> 00:50:38,211
You come highly recommended
by the Defense Department, Mr. Laurent.

573
00:50:38,281 --> 00:50:40,998
Though I'm unaware
of your personal qualifications.

574
00:50:41,065 --> 00:50:43,782
My men are ex-Delta Force. SEALs.

575
00:50:43,881 --> 00:50:46,531
I was formerly with the GIGN,
French Special Forces.

576
00:50:46,633 --> 00:50:48,804
I understand you had a corporate theft.

577
00:50:48,873 --> 00:50:51,207
Yes, that's what I told
the Defense Department.

578
00:50:51,272 --> 00:50:55,069
The reality is a little more complex.
That's why I require your services.

579
00:50:55,144 --> 00:50:58,144
We've had a... security breach.

580
00:50:58,216 --> 00:51:01,762
You have the Defense Department
at your disposal. Why call me?

581
00:51:01,832 --> 00:51:04,319
Because their
investment here is sizeable.

582
00:51:04,391 --> 00:51:07,555
One hundred and twenty
billion dollars, to be exact.

583
00:51:07,623 --> 00:51:10,438
And I can't afford
for them to reconsider.

584
00:51:10,503 --> 00:51:12,674
What you tell them
is your business, doctor.

585
00:51:12,743 --> 00:51:15,558
I am in the business
of keeping my clients' confidence.

586
00:51:15,655 --> 00:51:17,062
Good.

587
00:51:21,351 --> 00:51:23,587
Two of our products have escaped.

588
00:51:23,654 --> 00:51:26,524
Impressive,
considering they're vegetative.

589
00:51:26,598 --> 00:51:29,348
Well, after several years
of trial and error,

590
00:51:29,414 --> 00:51:31,683
we discovered that
without consciousness,

591
00:51:31,750 --> 00:51:36,965
without human experience,
emotion, without life,

592
00:51:37,029 --> 00:51:39,233
the organs failed.

593
00:51:40,806 --> 00:51:42,780
How long have they been missing?

594
00:51:42,853 --> 00:51:45,504
Four hours and 36 minutes.

595
00:51:45,573 --> 00:51:48,223
- They're on foot?
- Yes.

596
00:51:48,325 --> 00:51:52,034
Wade, 1.2 miles an hour,
five mile perimeter,

597
00:51:52,101 --> 00:51:55,068
- standby for suspect description.
- We're on it.

598
00:51:55,172 --> 00:51:56,546
Follow me.

599
00:52:12,740 --> 00:52:16,122
- Come on, we gotta keep going.
- I have to stop. I can't run anymore.

600
00:52:16,195 --> 00:52:17,439
- You gotta try.
- Where?

601
00:52:17,507 --> 00:52:19,928
- Anywhere but here.
- But there's nothing.

602
00:52:20,035 --> 00:52:22,685
Everything's dead, Lincoln.

603
00:52:28,099 --> 00:52:30,400
What if we are contaminated?

604
00:52:30,946 --> 00:52:32,953
Then we'd be dead.

605
00:52:33,698 --> 00:52:36,284
There's no contamination.
It was a lie.

606
00:52:47,105 --> 00:52:49,854
- What is it?
- I don't know.

607
00:52:49,921 --> 00:52:51,514
But it's alive.

608
00:52:55,969 --> 00:52:58,838
Come on. It's mean, whatever it is.

609
00:52:58,944 --> 00:53:00,155
Let's rest in here.

610
00:53:00,225 --> 00:53:02,875
Jordan Two Delta's sponsor,
Sarah Jordan, is in a coma

611
00:53:02,944 --> 00:53:05,977
after a car accident.
She's in need of multiple transplants.

612
00:53:06,048 --> 00:53:07,707
How long does she have?

613
00:53:07,776 --> 00:53:10,142
Forty-eight hours.
Three days maximum.

614
00:53:10,208 --> 00:53:11,866
Tell me about Six Echo.

615
00:53:11,936 --> 00:53:15,197
He was really the first one
to question his environment,

616
00:53:15,263 --> 00:53:16,725
his whole existence here.

617
00:53:16,800 --> 00:53:20,825
Over the last few months,
he began demonstrating unstable behavior

618
00:53:20,895 --> 00:53:23,612
and I can't account for it.

619
00:53:23,711 --> 00:53:26,078
I'm waiting on the result
of his synaptic scan.

620
00:53:26,175 --> 00:53:28,476
What do they know
about the outside world?

621
00:53:28,542 --> 00:53:30,397
Very little.

622
00:53:30,462 --> 00:53:33,429
We control them with
the memory of a shared event.

623
00:53:33,502 --> 00:53:37,692
A global contamination.
It keeps them fearful of going outside.

624
00:53:37,758 --> 00:53:42,133
The Island is the one thing
that gives them hope,

625
00:53:42,206 --> 00:53:44,148
gives them purpose.

626
00:53:44,669 --> 00:53:46,841
Everything we expose them to,

627
00:53:46,910 --> 00:53:50,390
their programs, their cartoons,
books, the games they play,

628
00:53:50,461 --> 00:53:53,941
are designed to manage aggression
and reinforce simple social skills.

629
00:53:54,013 --> 00:53:56,402
To avoid obvious complications,

630
00:53:56,509 --> 00:53:59,029
they aren't imprinted
with an awareness of sex.

631
00:53:59,133 --> 00:54:02,329
We find it simpler
to eliminate the drive altogether.

632
00:54:02,812 --> 00:54:07,929
In a very real sense...
they're like children.

633
00:54:07,996 --> 00:54:10,581
Educated to the level of a 15-year-old.

634
00:54:27,067 --> 00:54:30,296
- What was that?
- I don't know.

635
00:54:31,611 --> 00:54:33,269
But I want one.

636
00:54:47,290 --> 00:54:48,948
Look!

637
00:54:49,753 --> 00:54:52,917
Route 39. Route 39.

638
00:54:52,985 --> 00:54:54,895
Come on.

639
00:54:54,969 --> 00:54:57,042
I got it from a friend.

640
00:55:20,855 --> 00:55:22,797
I think that's it.

641
00:55:53,109 --> 00:55:54,189
What's up?

642
00:55:54,261 --> 00:55:56,814
Yeah, do you know
a guy named McCord?

643
00:55:58,389 --> 00:56:00,494
Yeah, we know that tool.
Who's asking?

644
00:56:01,333 --> 00:56:04,977
- I am.
- And you would be who?

645
00:56:05,077 --> 00:56:08,011
- Lincoln Six Echo.
- Jordan Two Delta.

646
00:56:09,268 --> 00:56:11,024
Right.

647
00:56:11,092 --> 00:56:13,842
Y'all some of those desert UFO freaks?

648
00:56:13,908 --> 00:56:16,875
- U... What? No, I don't think so.
- No.

649
00:56:16,948 --> 00:56:18,093
McCord?

650
00:56:18,164 --> 00:56:20,498
Well, lucky day, Captain Kirk.
He's in the can.

651
00:56:20,563 --> 00:56:22,865
- He's in a can?
- Taking a dump.

652
00:56:22,932 --> 00:56:24,655
A dump? Taking it where?

653
00:56:27,187 --> 00:56:29,423
Bubba, you're fixing
to get on my nerves.

654
00:56:29,491 --> 00:56:32,590
- It's the first door on the right.
- Thank you.

655
00:56:32,659 --> 00:56:35,593
I have to go.
He's taking a dump in a can.

656
00:56:35,699 --> 00:56:38,568
- Something to drink? Jack?
- Yes, please.

657
00:56:38,674 --> 00:56:40,584
Straight up?

658
00:56:51,122 --> 00:56:53,358
Oh, that is bitchin'.

659
00:56:55,537 --> 00:56:57,260
So this is Sector Five?

660
00:56:57,329 --> 00:56:59,533
Hey! You son of a bitch!

661
00:57:01,233 --> 00:57:02,891
You knew!

662
00:57:02,961 --> 00:57:06,059
- How the hell did you get out?
- Why do they lie to us? Tell me!

663
00:57:06,129 --> 00:57:07,885
They're gonna be looking for you.

664
00:57:07,985 --> 00:57:11,050
- Tell me what's going on!
- If anybody sees us together,

665
00:57:11,152 --> 00:57:13,159
both of us are gonna be dead.

666
00:57:13,264 --> 00:57:16,013
So, will you just
take your hands off me? Let me...

667
00:57:16,080 --> 00:57:20,204
Let me pull my pants up
and I'll take you back to my place

668
00:57:20,272 --> 00:57:21,995
so we can be alone. OK?

669
00:57:24,912 --> 00:57:28,207
- Ed.
- Mac.

670
00:57:29,072 --> 00:57:31,373
Give you... give you boys a minute?

671
00:57:32,783 --> 00:57:35,204
What?
This isn't what it looks like.

672
00:57:37,295 --> 00:57:39,400
Sure. Sure.

673
00:57:39,502 --> 00:57:41,325
Get out of here, you stupid...

674
00:57:41,391 --> 00:57:43,463
Will you stop?

675
00:57:44,846 --> 00:57:48,141
You can'tjust bust in on a guy
like that. That's really rude.

676
00:57:49,230 --> 00:57:51,685
She doesn't understand the licking.

677
00:57:51,757 --> 00:57:54,059
You a knucklehead?
You brought another one?

678
00:57:54,126 --> 00:57:56,100
- Excuse me.
- Hey. Hey, hey! Hey, hey!

679
00:57:56,173 --> 00:57:58,508
Back off, Joe, OK?
Don't push me!

680
00:57:58,574 --> 00:58:00,035
No, no, no, that's no good.

681
00:58:00,109 --> 00:58:01,570
Put it on my tab.
We gotta go.

682
00:58:01,645 --> 00:58:04,067
Friends from out of town.
Come on, sweetheart.

683
00:58:04,141 --> 00:58:05,896
- Give me your number.
- Two Delta.

684
00:58:05,965 --> 00:58:08,550
Hey, look. Get...
Don't test me.

685
00:58:08,621 --> 00:58:10,508
Don't.

686
00:58:21,836 --> 00:58:24,454
Well, this is nice.

687
00:58:27,179 --> 00:58:29,961
Mac doesn't talk much
about his work at the Institute.

688
00:58:30,027 --> 00:58:32,329
Do y'all work with him?

689
00:58:33,419 --> 00:58:36,321
Saving lives and all
must be real rewarding.

690
00:58:36,395 --> 00:58:38,696
Those are fancy tracksuits.

691
00:58:38,763 --> 00:58:42,341
Y'all exercise out in this heat,
gonna get yourself nasty heatstroke.

692
00:58:43,275 --> 00:58:46,755
Oh, Mac, look.
They got matching bracelets.

693
00:58:46,858 --> 00:58:50,633
- We should do that, honey.
- Suzie...

694
00:58:50,698 --> 00:58:53,698
Do you remember the talk
we had about all the talk?

695
00:58:54,954 --> 00:58:56,066
Yeah.

696
00:58:56,137 --> 00:58:59,366
Actually, would you run down to Red's
and pick us up a sixer of Bud?

697
00:58:59,433 --> 00:59:02,630
- We've got to talk shop.
- OK, baby.

698
00:59:02,697 --> 00:59:04,933
- Just making friends.
- I know. Good. Just...

699
00:59:05,001 --> 00:59:06,211
Bye.

700
00:59:12,329 --> 00:59:13,670
Why do they lie, Mac?

701
00:59:13,737 --> 00:59:16,289
Why do they lie to us? Tell me.

702
00:59:19,688 --> 00:59:21,728
To keep you
from knowing what you are.

703
00:59:22,504 --> 00:59:25,984
- What we are?
- What are we?

704
00:59:26,056 --> 00:59:29,917
Man, why do I gotta be the guy
tells the kids there's no Santa Claus?

705
00:59:33,991 --> 00:59:36,162
OK, look. You're...

706
00:59:38,503 --> 00:59:40,642
Well, you're not like me.

707
00:59:42,375 --> 00:59:45,440
I mean, you're not... human.

708
00:59:46,822 --> 00:59:50,816
I mean, you're human,
but you just, you're not real.

709
00:59:50,918 --> 00:59:54,627
You're not,
like, a real person. Like me.

710
00:59:57,669 --> 00:59:59,906
You're clones.

711
01:00:01,861 --> 01:00:05,538
You're copies of people
out here in the world.

712
01:00:05,605 --> 01:00:07,165
- What?
- Clones?

713
01:00:07,237 --> 01:00:09,342
- What? Why?
- What are you talking about?

714
01:00:09,413 --> 01:00:12,642
Some hag trophy wife
needs new skin for a facelift

715
01:00:12,709 --> 01:00:14,781
or one of 'em gets sick
and need a new part,

716
01:00:14,852 --> 01:00:17,089
they take it from you.

717
01:00:18,692 --> 01:00:21,791
But I have a mother.
I remember her.

718
01:00:21,892 --> 01:00:23,867
- Yeah, I know.
- I grew up on a farm.

719
01:00:23,972 --> 01:00:25,914
I have a little dog and I had a bike.

720
01:00:26,020 --> 01:00:27,481
And a bike. Right.

721
01:00:27,588 --> 01:00:30,849
It was a pink Flexi-Flyer
with little tassels on the handlebars

722
01:00:30,915 --> 01:00:33,020
and you rode it
to your grandmother's.

723
01:00:33,091 --> 01:00:36,222
You ring the little bell and she
came out and served you cookies.

724
01:00:36,291 --> 01:00:37,568
Yeah.

725
01:00:37,635 --> 01:00:41,661
No. Memory imprints.
I seen them.

726
01:00:41,731 --> 01:00:44,797
A buddy of mine is a programmer
at the Institute. He showed me.

727
01:00:44,867 --> 01:00:48,314
There's only 12 stories.
They change around little details,

728
01:00:48,386 --> 01:00:50,524
but they're all pretty much the same.

729
01:00:50,594 --> 01:00:55,809
The life you think you had
before the "contamination,"

730
01:00:55,874 --> 01:00:58,208
it never happened.

731
01:00:59,426 --> 01:01:02,906
Come on, don't look at me like that.
At least you had a bike.

732
01:01:02,978 --> 01:01:06,971
Wanna trade your rosy memory implants
for my shitty childhood, be my guest.

733
01:01:07,041 --> 01:01:08,535
How long?

734
01:01:09,569 --> 01:01:11,162
How long have we been alive?

735
01:01:12,289 --> 01:01:15,103
You're Echo generation,
so you're three.

736
01:01:16,705 --> 01:01:18,166
Delta means you're four.

737
01:01:20,576 --> 01:01:21,754
Three?

738
01:01:21,825 --> 01:01:25,621
The whole reason you exist is
'cause everyone wants to live forever.

739
01:01:25,728 --> 01:01:27,484
It's the new American dream.

740
01:01:27,552 --> 01:01:30,900
There's people out there that are
rich enough to pay anything for it.

741
01:01:31,008 --> 01:01:34,357
Don't people care that they kill us?
That they take parts from us?

742
01:01:34,431 --> 01:01:38,522
They don't know. They think you're
vegetables simmering in a jelly sack.

743
01:01:38,591 --> 01:01:42,934
Why do you think Merrick has you stuck
in an old military bunker below ground?

744
01:01:43,007 --> 01:01:46,585
He doesn't want anybody knowing
the truth, especially not sponsors.

745
01:01:46,655 --> 01:01:50,364
- Sponsors?
- The people that had you made.

746
01:01:50,430 --> 01:01:52,502
They, like, own you.

747
01:01:54,494 --> 01:02:00,157
But why doesn't Merrick want
our owners to know that we're alive?

748
01:02:00,222 --> 01:02:04,761
Just because people wanna eat the burger
doesn't mean they wanna meet the cow.

749
01:02:05,630 --> 01:02:09,175
Besides, do you know
how many laws Merrick's breaking

750
01:02:09,245 --> 01:02:11,384
to have you two hatched?

751
01:02:13,117 --> 01:02:15,288
Your sponsors
can't have any part of that.

752
01:02:15,357 --> 01:02:17,658
They're like high society,
rich and famous.

753
01:02:17,725 --> 01:02:20,146
If they knew,
Merrick would be out of business.

754
01:02:20,221 --> 01:02:22,741
We have to find our sponsors
and tell them the truth.

755
01:02:22,813 --> 01:02:24,122
- What?
- Yeah.

756
01:02:24,188 --> 01:02:26,195
No, that's the worst idea I ever heard.

757
01:02:26,268 --> 01:02:28,657
You know how dead I'd be?
Not to mention fired?

758
01:02:28,764 --> 01:02:31,001
We will. We will.
That's our only chance.

759
01:02:31,068 --> 01:02:33,915
Stop, stop! Fold, stop.
Brakes. No. Come on.

760
01:02:33,979 --> 01:02:36,597
You're the replacement engines
on their Bentley.

761
01:02:36,667 --> 01:02:39,831
They're not gonna care.
What? They're gonna care?

762
01:02:39,899 --> 01:02:41,175
You know what I would do?

763
01:02:41,243 --> 01:02:44,472
I would just get as far away
from here as I could.

764
01:02:44,539 --> 01:02:45,716
Go to the beach.

765
01:02:45,787 --> 01:02:48,820
We're not asking
for your permission, Mac.

766
01:02:48,890 --> 01:02:50,745
We're asking for your help.

767
01:02:52,251 --> 01:02:54,007
Oh, God.

768
01:03:02,010 --> 01:03:06,287
Infrared's having a hard time picking up
a heat signature. Sand's too hot.

769
01:03:10,329 --> 01:03:12,850
He was implanted
with micro-sensors yesterday.

770
01:03:12,921 --> 01:03:16,631
Can we configure our instrument
to pick up a low-frequency RF scan?

771
01:03:16,697 --> 01:03:19,861
- If we can get within half a mile.
- Do it.

772
01:03:19,929 --> 01:03:22,612
Your sponsors names
are Tom Lincoln and Sarah Jordan.

773
01:03:22,681 --> 01:03:24,274
Her sponsor lives in New York.

774
01:03:24,345 --> 01:03:27,247
The number in your name
is a regional code.

775
01:03:27,321 --> 01:03:31,444
Six Echo, that means
your sponsor lives in LA.

776
01:03:31,544 --> 01:03:33,584
- You're going out of state.
- Out of state?

777
01:03:33,688 --> 01:03:35,117
Put this on.

778
01:03:35,223 --> 01:03:38,093
You're gonna go in here.
All right? Come on, come on.

779
01:03:38,199 --> 01:03:40,817
Keep going. What size?

780
01:03:41,720 --> 01:03:43,094
All right.

781
01:03:43,159 --> 01:03:45,231
These are bags, OK?
You put stuff in 'em.

782
01:03:45,303 --> 01:03:47,954
Backpacks for boys, purses for girls.
Understand?

783
01:03:48,023 --> 01:03:49,452
We're not idiots.

784
01:03:49,527 --> 01:03:52,843
Excuse me, Miss "I'm so smart
I can't wait to go to the Island."

785
01:03:56,310 --> 01:03:58,252
Yeah. Good.

786
01:04:03,350 --> 01:04:04,561
Wait. Hold, hold, hold.

787
01:04:04,662 --> 01:04:07,029
People don't really
wear these on the outside.

788
01:04:07,126 --> 01:04:09,581
These are mail-order, OK?
These stay here.

789
01:04:12,373 --> 01:04:16,148
No. Mail-order, OK?
Clones don't wear these.

790
01:04:19,765 --> 01:04:21,009
All right, listen up.

791
01:04:21,077 --> 01:04:24,012
This card is like stim credits, OK?

792
01:04:24,084 --> 01:04:26,932
Lt'll get you food, but I gotta
report it stolen in 24 hours

793
01:04:26,997 --> 01:04:30,925
or else they'll know I helped you.
After that, use the cash.

794
01:04:33,876 --> 01:04:34,923
All right, look.

795
01:04:35,028 --> 01:04:37,898
I know you're new to this
whole human experience and all,

796
01:04:38,004 --> 01:04:39,630
but there's one universal truth

797
01:04:39,731 --> 01:04:42,382
and that is you never
give a woman your credit card.

798
01:04:43,123 --> 01:04:45,032
Right.

799
01:04:50,771 --> 01:04:52,396
I got something. It's hot.

800
01:05:02,611 --> 01:05:05,066
Oh, God.

801
01:05:06,802 --> 01:05:09,737
- Train four...
- Train'll be here. Hustle.

802
01:05:09,810 --> 01:05:13,225
...to Sacramento
is now boarding at platform A.

803
01:05:13,297 --> 01:05:16,942
All right, stay. All right?
Just stay. Don't move.

804
01:05:18,033 --> 01:05:19,440
Mama!

805
01:05:23,089 --> 01:05:24,976
Look at that!

806
01:05:25,041 --> 01:05:27,212
Those are kids.

807
01:05:28,944 --> 01:05:30,406
Wow.

808
01:05:35,888 --> 01:05:39,204
Come here. The train is non-stop to LA.
You need these to get on.

809
01:05:39,280 --> 01:05:42,793
When you get there, look up your
sponsors in the information directory.

810
01:05:42,864 --> 01:05:44,271
- You got it?
- Yeah. Yeah.

811
01:05:44,336 --> 01:05:47,980
- What is an information directory?
- It'll tell you where they live.

812
01:05:48,080 --> 01:05:50,927
And whatever you do,
do not trust anyone.

813
01:05:50,991 --> 01:05:54,919
One thing I can tell you about people,
is that they'll do anything to survive.

814
01:05:54,991 --> 01:05:56,878
Thank you, Mac. Thank you.

815
01:05:57,742 --> 01:05:59,564
Thanks a lot.

816
01:05:59,630 --> 01:06:03,045
All right. I'm just gonna go upstairs
and get you guys a map of LA.

817
01:06:03,118 --> 01:06:05,387
Better not get me in trouble.

818
01:06:16,110 --> 01:06:18,979
Yeah, no problem.
Sure, that's a good one.

819
01:06:26,188 --> 01:06:28,425
I think I got an ID.
Two in the center.

820
01:06:34,444 --> 01:06:36,965
Run!

821
01:08:08,135 --> 01:08:09,661
Run!

822
01:08:12,390 --> 01:08:13,502
God!

823
01:08:16,070 --> 01:08:20,926
Amtrak train 227 now departing
for Los Angeles at platform C.

824
01:08:25,957 --> 01:08:28,805
What's wrong with these people?
They killed him.

825
01:08:42,564 --> 01:08:45,411
- This was supposed to be a simple job?
- It's never simple.

826
01:08:45,475 --> 01:08:47,068
We got a missing credit card.

827
01:08:47,140 --> 01:08:51,395
McCord just used it to buy train tickets
and it's not in his wallet.

828
01:08:51,460 --> 01:08:55,518
Monitor the account. Have Amtrak
patch you through to the conductor.

829
01:08:56,611 --> 01:08:58,400
Get me a new team in LA.

830
01:09:01,091 --> 01:09:03,905
- Got here as fast as I could.
- Come here.

831
01:09:03,970 --> 01:09:07,036
I finished scanning the Defense
Department Troop Selections,

832
01:09:07,106 --> 01:09:09,626
- if you want to see them...
- Not yet. Look at that.

833
01:09:11,331 --> 01:09:14,265
- Six Echo drew it.
- It's elaborate.

834
01:09:14,338 --> 01:09:18,396
"Renovachio." Renovatee-oh?

835
01:09:18,466 --> 01:09:20,888
Renovatio.
What is that, Italian?

836
01:09:20,962 --> 01:09:22,871
It's Latin.

837
01:09:23,298 --> 01:09:25,403
We've never imprinted
an agnate with Latin.

838
01:09:25,474 --> 01:09:27,677
Yes, I'm well aware of that.

839
01:09:28,514 --> 01:09:30,782
So where did he learn it?

840
01:09:30,881 --> 01:09:32,791
Where are the results from his scan?

841
01:09:32,897 --> 01:09:36,606
- They'll be back from Johns Hopkins...
- Just speed it up.

842
01:09:36,673 --> 01:09:37,687
Yes, sir.

843
01:09:50,208 --> 01:09:51,156
You two.

844
01:09:51,232 --> 01:09:53,566
Ladies and gentlemen,
your attention please,

845
01:09:53,631 --> 01:09:56,598
train number 17
leaving for San Diego...

846
01:09:56,671 --> 01:09:59,126
- There!
...was delayed 20 minutes. Stand by.

847
01:11:43,320 --> 01:11:46,800
We just arrived, but Troy's already
tapped into the city cameras.

848
01:11:53,592 --> 01:11:57,039
Excuse me.
Where's an information directory?

849
01:11:57,111 --> 01:11:58,573
Thanks.

850
01:12:03,959 --> 01:12:06,807
Wilshire. 5th. Grand.

851
01:12:06,871 --> 01:12:11,605
Spring. Grand Avenue?
Smile for the camera, sweetheart.

852
01:12:19,542 --> 01:12:22,738
Where is Flower?
You on Flower?

853
01:12:23,318 --> 01:12:26,068
Olive, Olive.
Come on, come on.

854
01:12:26,134 --> 01:12:28,108
You look familiar.

855
01:12:28,662 --> 01:12:29,774
Gotcha.

856
01:12:32,118 --> 01:12:34,485
Three Black Wasps
and two jet bikes.

857
01:12:34,549 --> 01:12:36,938
We just got a facial hit
on our fugitives!

858
01:12:37,013 --> 01:12:39,118
Let's go! Let's go! Move!

859
01:12:42,549 --> 01:12:44,491
We're moving! Let's go.

860
01:12:55,732 --> 01:12:57,674
Wait. Got a hit
on McCord's credit card.

861
01:12:57,748 --> 01:13:00,203
Location, Grand Avenue at 9830.

862
01:13:00,275 --> 01:13:02,926
Team, proceed immediately to 9830.

863
01:13:02,995 --> 01:13:06,889
No, no, no. LAPD's moving in.
They've flagged McCord's credit card.

864
01:13:06,963 --> 01:13:09,997
- Tom Lincoln.
- One moment, please.

865
01:13:11,251 --> 01:13:14,480
- Not listed.
- Sarah Jordan.

866
01:13:21,042 --> 01:13:22,122
Hello?

867
01:13:22,194 --> 01:13:25,128
Yes, I'm looking for Sarah Jordan.

868
01:13:25,746 --> 01:13:28,047
She's sick.

869
01:13:28,114 --> 01:13:32,074
- Can I talk to her?
- She's at the hospital.

870
01:13:32,145 --> 01:13:34,447
Mommy, is that you?

871
01:13:49,648 --> 01:13:51,885
Jordan. Let's go!

872
01:13:54,192 --> 01:13:56,047
Freeze! Put your hands up!

873
01:13:56,112 --> 01:13:58,414
- Keep your hands off!
- Put your hands up!

874
01:13:58,480 --> 01:14:00,389
Do as I say! Do as I say!

875
01:14:01,648 --> 01:14:03,852
- Lincoln.
- Just do what they say.

876
01:14:03,920 --> 01:14:05,327
Lincoln.

877
01:14:05,391 --> 01:14:06,536
- Pull back.
- Move out.

878
01:14:06,607 --> 01:14:08,200
What's going on?

879
01:14:16,687 --> 01:14:18,858
Nail it! Quick, move!

880
01:14:29,038 --> 01:14:32,201
We're detaining you in connection
to the murder of James McCord.

881
01:14:32,269 --> 01:14:35,303
- What? He was my friend!
- Anything you say can and will be used

882
01:14:35,374 --> 01:14:37,959
- against you in a court of law.
- What's a court of law?

883
01:14:41,421 --> 01:14:44,552
They'll run DNA.
If the agnates are booked,

884
01:14:44,621 --> 01:14:47,523
it'll implicate your clients
in a murder investigation.

885
01:14:47,597 --> 01:14:48,774
This is a nightmare.

886
01:14:48,877 --> 01:14:51,659
You cannot allow this to happen.
Do you understand me?

887
01:14:51,724 --> 01:14:54,026
You use any force that is necessary.

888
01:14:54,092 --> 01:14:56,547
I'm ordering you
to contain the situation.

889
01:14:56,652 --> 01:14:59,751
1-Adam-82, we've apprehended
the suspects. Two adults, no ID.

890
01:14:59,820 --> 01:15:02,373
Notify Forensics,
we'll need DNA typing.

891
01:15:02,444 --> 01:15:04,810
- My name is Tom Lincoln.
- Sit back and shut up.

892
01:15:04,876 --> 01:15:07,942
- Could you look up my file, please?
- Sit back.

893
01:15:22,219 --> 01:15:24,837
Dispatch, we're two minutes out.

894
01:15:34,186 --> 01:15:36,160
- Check inside!
- Hey, can you hear me?

895
01:15:36,233 --> 01:15:39,200
Lincoln, get up!
Get up, Lincoln! Get up!

896
01:15:45,577 --> 01:15:46,689
Let's go!

897
01:15:47,337 --> 01:15:49,028
Go! Go! Go!

898
01:15:49,801 --> 01:15:50,848
Go!

899
01:15:54,441 --> 01:15:56,001
We got cops. We got cops!

900
01:16:03,400 --> 01:16:04,677
Get down!

901
01:16:11,847 --> 01:16:13,734
Run!

902
01:16:14,407 --> 01:16:16,928
I see them! Let's get moving!

903
01:16:18,151 --> 01:16:20,769
Let's go!
Come on, come on, come on!

904
01:16:21,671 --> 01:16:23,012
Move, move!

905
01:16:23,079 --> 01:16:24,834
Move out! Move out!

906
01:16:35,238 --> 01:16:36,929
Come on!

907
01:16:45,413 --> 01:16:47,999
Go, go, go, go! Go!

908
01:16:58,596 --> 01:17:00,451
Shit! Check up here!

909
01:17:01,605 --> 01:17:02,979
Come on!

910
01:17:37,698 --> 01:17:40,697
Air-Two, give me status of the targets.

911
01:17:41,410 --> 01:17:44,508
- Targets are under the train wheels.
- Silently, take them out.

912
01:17:47,361 --> 01:17:48,376
Go!

913
01:17:51,137 --> 01:17:52,860
Move! Go, go!

914
01:17:52,929 --> 01:17:54,423
- I can't fit!
- Move back!

915
01:17:54,497 --> 01:17:55,707
I can't fit!

916
01:18:13,311 --> 01:18:14,740
Look out, look out!

917
01:18:20,767 --> 01:18:22,109
Right, right, right!

918
01:18:36,254 --> 01:18:37,236
Stay on them!

919
01:18:39,422 --> 01:18:40,829
Look out!

920
01:18:45,149 --> 01:18:47,767
Do not let him get away!
Do not let him get away!

921
01:19:09,564 --> 01:19:11,255
Good job!

922
01:19:12,636 --> 01:19:15,931
We've gotta bail out of here,
there's police choppers inbound.

923
01:19:24,251 --> 01:19:26,073
Black Wasp, take out the truck!

924
01:19:36,378 --> 01:19:38,483
Troy, you all right? Let's go!

925
01:19:43,066 --> 01:19:44,048
Cops! Cops!

926
01:20:06,904 --> 01:20:08,148
He's coming back!

927
01:20:10,712 --> 01:20:11,890
Stay down, Jordan!

928
01:20:38,966 --> 01:20:42,282
- How do you know what you're doing?
- I don't know!

929
01:21:38,867 --> 01:21:40,110
Hold on!

930
01:21:41,970 --> 01:21:43,082
Look out!

931
01:21:50,162 --> 01:21:51,339
Look out!

932
01:21:58,641 --> 01:22:00,812
Hold on!

933
01:22:17,968 --> 01:22:20,783
- Don't let me go, Lincoln!
- I got you! I got you!

934
01:22:20,848 --> 01:22:22,888
- Don't let me go!
- I got you!

935
01:22:23,599 --> 01:22:26,861
I'm slipping!
Don't drop me, Lincoln!

936
01:22:26,960 --> 01:22:30,123
- Don't drop me!
- I got you! I got you!

937
01:22:33,103 --> 01:22:36,102
Lincoln! Pull me! Pull me!

938
01:22:37,871 --> 01:22:39,878
Climb up!

939
01:22:42,766 --> 01:22:45,384
If there's no way to get
our fugitives quietly,

940
01:22:45,454 --> 01:22:47,626
you need to take them out.

941
01:22:50,734 --> 01:22:52,872
I see our targets about 70 stories up.

942
01:22:52,974 --> 01:22:55,275
They're on top of the building logo.

943
01:22:58,606 --> 01:23:00,231
Tough day.

944
01:23:00,878 --> 01:23:02,252
Let's roll.

945
01:23:03,821 --> 01:23:05,959
LAPD! Get away from the window!

946
01:23:10,157 --> 01:23:11,204
Jay, you got him?

947
01:23:12,845 --> 01:23:14,699
Right there! Right there!
Get him!

948
01:23:22,859 --> 01:23:25,729
Stay there! Damn it!
Just stay down!

949
01:23:26,284 --> 01:23:27,778
Come on!

950
01:23:31,275 --> 01:23:33,828
Gonna swing around to get a shot.

951
01:23:39,659 --> 01:23:40,968
He's coming back.

952
01:23:56,426 --> 01:23:57,538
Oh, no.

953
01:24:01,129 --> 01:24:03,464
Hang on!
They're coming off the building.

954
01:24:28,807 --> 01:24:30,563
Look out!

955
01:24:45,414 --> 01:24:46,876
Jesus must love you!

956
01:24:46,950 --> 01:24:49,219
That was the craziest mess
I ever seen!

957
01:24:49,286 --> 01:24:52,799
Come on, girl.
I know Jesus loves you.

958
01:25:02,405 --> 01:25:04,958
Can you keep a secret, doc?

959
01:25:05,029 --> 01:25:06,589
Why, yes, of course.

960
01:25:06,661 --> 01:25:08,832
There is something
going on around here.

961
01:25:08,901 --> 01:25:11,105
Something you may
not even know about.

962
01:25:11,173 --> 01:25:12,188
What is it?

963
01:25:12,261 --> 01:25:17,247
Well, I'm not sure that
the contamination is real.

964
01:25:17,317 --> 01:25:19,226
- Why do you think that?
- OK.

965
01:25:19,301 --> 01:25:24,003
Lincoln told me that he found
a flying bug in Sector Six.

966
01:25:24,068 --> 01:25:25,529
- Wow.
- Right.

967
01:25:25,604 --> 01:25:28,386
And I think that might be why
he thought he could leave.

968
01:25:28,452 --> 01:25:31,005
Have you told
anyone else about this?

969
01:25:31,108 --> 01:25:34,882
No, no. But I'm gonna do some digging.
I'm gonna get to the bottom of this.

970
01:25:34,979 --> 01:25:37,597
And when I do,
I'll share my information with you.

971
01:25:37,667 --> 01:25:39,260
Thank you.

972
01:25:39,331 --> 01:25:41,469
I want to be helpful.
I like it here.

973
01:25:41,539 --> 01:25:43,263
Good.

974
01:25:43,331 --> 01:25:45,698
But I really want to look
into the lottery too.

975
01:25:45,763 --> 01:25:48,730
- Something's wrong there.
- Yeah.

976
01:25:48,803 --> 01:25:50,559
You know,

977
01:25:50,627 --> 01:25:53,082
you were one of the first
of the Echo generation.

978
01:25:53,155 --> 01:25:55,259
You're very smart.

979
01:25:55,330 --> 01:25:57,916
Yeah. I remember
when I first came here.

980
01:26:00,514 --> 01:26:03,099
A survivor, just like you.

981
01:26:03,202 --> 01:26:05,689
One of the first, in fact.

982
01:26:05,794 --> 01:26:09,568
It's natural, even healthy,
to question the world we're presented.

983
01:26:09,665 --> 01:26:12,960
You might say it's only...
only human.

984
01:26:15,329 --> 01:26:17,750
Oh, that burns!

985
01:26:19,456 --> 01:26:23,034
Get me a list of all the Echos
in active population.

986
01:26:40,000 --> 01:26:42,366
I saw his address. Tom Lincoln.

987
01:26:42,463 --> 01:26:45,245
We'll go there when the rain stops.

988
01:26:45,855 --> 01:26:48,855
- It'll be OK when we find him.
- OK.

989
01:26:54,174 --> 01:26:56,989
That little boy looked like me.

990
01:26:59,998 --> 01:27:02,267
His mom's gonna die, isn't she?

991
01:27:03,358 --> 01:27:04,983
I don't know.

992
01:27:07,741 --> 01:27:09,334
You're lying.

993
01:27:16,765 --> 01:27:18,652
It's cold.

994
01:28:06,522 --> 01:28:07,667
Go in.

995
01:28:08,377 --> 01:28:09,654
I can't.

996
01:28:10,457 --> 01:28:13,806
- I'll go in.
- Jordan. Jordan!

997
01:28:17,305 --> 01:28:19,029
Hello?

998
01:28:21,689 --> 01:28:23,445
Hello?

999
01:29:09,238 --> 01:29:10,831
Lincoln!

1000
01:29:27,253 --> 01:29:29,424
Oh, my God.

1001
01:29:31,604 --> 01:29:34,255
